The function keeps only the public columns from each row, so the docstring should say that and note that personal fields are excluded. [tool_use propose_change {"path":"register/export.py","summary":"Add docstring to export_comments describing its input, output, and the public-column filtering.","diff":"--- a/register/export.py\n+++ b/register/export.py\n@@ -4,6 +4,20 @@\n PUBLIC_COLUMNS = ['reference', 'address', 'comment_date', 'stance', 'comment_text']\n \n def export_comments(rows):\n+    \"\"\"Return public-facing copies of comment rows for export.\n+\n+    Each row is reduced to the columns in PUBLIC_COLUMNS (reference, address,\n+    comment_date, stance, comment_text). All other fields, including objector\n+    name, email, phone and internal_note, are dropped and never included in the\n+    output.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        rows: An iterable of mappings, each containing at least the PUBLIC_COLUMNS keys.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        A list of dicts, one per input row, containing only the public columns.\n+        Raises KeyError if a row is missing one of the public columns.\n+    \"\"\"\n     out = []\n     for row in rows:\n         out.append({c: row[c] for c in PUBLIC_COLUMNS})\n"}]
